-- תקנון שירות עובדי הוראה, פרק 3, §3.3 הגדרת תפקידים
-- The elementary-school teacher's duties: teaching and planning, records and
-- grades, the pedagogical councils, duty rosters and punctuality, class
-- education, parents, substitution, confidentiality, pupils' discipline,
-- training, gifts, private lessons, smoking, and the press.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT common

§ `3.3 הגדרת תפקידים`

DECLARE `3.3 party` IS ONE OF
    `a takanon party` HAS `who` IS A Party
    `the teaching staff`
    `the pedagogical council`

DECLARE `teacher's act` IS ONE OF
    `shape the school by section 2 of the State Education Law`
    `work for the pupils' progress`
    `impart the subject and sound work and study habits`
    `improve own work and knowledge`
    `plan the year's work as a whole, by trimesters`
    `record the trimester's planning`
    `note why the plan was not covered and what was`
    `prepare each lesson, use fitting teaching aids, suit methods to the pupils and attend to those who struggle`
    `keep an orderly work diary`
    `plan the homework, continuing or preparing the lessons, with a clear learning goal`
    `submit the work diary to the supervisor and the principal for review`
    `hold written work and tests by the school's procedure, return them corrected in reasonable time and report them to the principal`
    `give the class educator the grades in writing, at the school's times and by its arrangements`
    `give the principal general assessments of each pupil's achievements`
    `keep records of the pupils' achievements as the basis of the grades`
    `make the achievement records available to the principal`
    `attend the pedagogical council`
    `tell the principal in advance of a justified absence from the council`
    `attend a meeting the principal called for a special need`
    `take into account a part-time teacher's ability to attend`
    `follow the pedagogical council's decisions`
    `reconsider the disagreement with the supervisor present`
    `attend the small pedagogical council`
    `do the duty roster the principal set`
    `be at school before the start` HAS `minutes before` IS A NUMBER
    `take part, as part of her work, in the activities the school organises for its pupils`
    `accept the post of class educator`
    `receive parents and report on achievements`
    `answer parents or outsiders during lessons`
    `answer parents or outsiders at another time she did not set in advance`
    `substitute for a missing teacher`
    `stay at school in the freed hours at the principal's disposal and substitute as needed`
    `disclose the pedagogical council's discussions to a non-member without the principal's consent`
    `disclose details about pupils to anyone but the principal, the class educator or the parents or guardians`
    `issue a confirmation or document that may be seen as the school's without the principal's consent`
    `invite guests or visitors to the school or class without the principal's approval`
    `notify the principal of an absence`
    `refer the pupil to the class educator or the school's management`
    `send a pupil home during lessons without the principal's consent and notice to the parents`
    `send a pupil home for homework, lateness or a donation`
    `lower a grade as a punishment`
    `follow the Ministry's guidelines, the principal and the council`
    `take part in training in free time`
    `accept from pupils or parents a gift of benefit that is not a symbolic token of thanks`
    `give paid private lessons to pupils of her school` HAS `with the supervisor's approval` IS A BOOLEAN
    `teach organised school groups for pay` HAS `with the supervisor's leave` IS A BOOLEAN
    `smoke in the institution before the pupils while on duty`
    `publish in the press information on her work, post or institution, directly or through another, named or not, without leave of the director-general or his delegate`
    `write articles or publish books on her educational work, keeping confidentiality`
    `pass news of the institution to the spokesman through the district manager`

-- A duty or a prohibition on the teacher, as most clauses of 3.3 are, and
-- the principal's duty in 9.
GIVEN `the act` IS A `teacher's act`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `the teacher must` `the act` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    MUST  a PROVIDED a EQUALS `the act`
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "3.3: a teacher's duty"

GIVEN `the act` IS A `teacher's act`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `the teacher shall not` `the act` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    SHANT a PROVIDED a EQUALS `the act`
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "3.3: a teacher's prohibition"

GIVEN `the act` IS A `teacher's act`
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `the principal must` `the act` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the school principal`
    MUST  a PROVIDED a EQUALS `the act`
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the school principal` BECAUSE "3.3: the principal's duty"

§§ `1-8 Teaching`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_1 akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_1/p2
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.1 the staff shape the school` IS
    PARTY `the teaching staff`
    MUST  `shape the school by section 2 of the State Education Law`
    LEST  BREACH BY `the teaching staff` BECAUSE "3.3.1: the teaching staff shape the school on the principles of section 2 of the State Education Law"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_2__subpara_a
`3.3.2א the pupils' progress` MEANS `the teacher must` `work for the pupils' progress`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_2__subpara_b
`3.3.2ב the subject and habits` MEANS `the teacher must` `impart the subject and sound work and study habits`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_3
`3.3.3 self-improvement` MEANS `the teacher must` `improve own work and knowledge`

-- 4: a whole-year plan, by trimesters; its details recorded at the start of
-- each trimester; where the trimester's material was not all covered, the
-- reason and what was covered noted at its end. Time in trimesters.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_4
GIVEN `covered all the material planned for the trimester` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.4 planning` `covered all the material planned for the trimester` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `plan the year's work as a whole, by trimesters`
    HENCE (PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
           MUST  `record the trimester's planning`
           WITHIN 0
           HENCE (IF `covered all the material planned for the trimester`
                  THEN FULFILLED
                  ELSE PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
                       MUST  `note why the plan was not covered and what was`
                       WITHIN 1
                       LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "3.3.4: what was not covered is noted with its reason at the trimester's end")
           LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "3.3.4: the trimester's planning is recorded at its start")
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "3.3.4: the year's work is planned as a whole, by trimesters"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_5
`3.3.5 preparing each lesson` MEANS `the teacher must` `prepare each lesson, use fitting teaching aids, suit methods to the pupils and attend to those who struggle`

-- 6: a teacher on probation keeps an orderly work diary (the material and how
-- it was taught), plans the homework given at the end of the lesson — a
-- continuation of the lesson or a preparation for the next, with a clear
-- goal — and submits the diary to the supervisor and the principal if asked.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_6
GIVEN `on probation` IS A BOOLEAN, `asked to submit it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.6 the work diary` `on probation` `asked to submit it` IS
    IF `on probation`
    THEN `the teacher must` `keep an orderly work diary`
         RAND `the teacher must` `plan the homework, continuing or preparing the lessons, with a clear learning goal`
         RAND (IF `asked to submit it` THEN `the teacher must` `submit the work diary to the supervisor and the principal for review` ELSE FULFILLED)
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_7
`3.3.7 written work` MEANS `the teacher must` `hold written work and tests by the school's procedure, return them corrected in reasonable time and report them to the principal`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_8__subpara_a
GIVEN `the principal asks for assessments` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.8א grades and assessments` `the principal asks for assessments` IS
    `the teacher must` `give the class educator the grades in writing, at the school's times and by its arrangements`
    RAND (IF `the principal asks for assessments` THEN `the teacher must` `give the principal general assessments of each pupil's achievements` ELSE FULFILLED)

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_8__subpara_b
GIVEN `the principal asks for the records` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.8ב achievement records` `the principal asks for the records` IS
    `the teacher must` `keep records of the pupils' achievements as the basis of the grades`
    RAND (IF `the principal asks for the records` THEN `the teacher must` `make the achievement records available to the principal` ELSE FULFILLED)

§§ `9-13 The pedagogical councils`

-- 9: every teacher attends the pedagogical council; one who cannot, for good
-- reason, tells the principal in advance. (10 limits it for a teacher of
-- under half a position; the two together are below.)
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_9
GIVEN `a justified reason to miss it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.9 the pedagogical council` `a justified reason to miss it` IS
    IF `a justified reason to miss it`
    THEN `the teacher must` `tell the principal in advance of a justified absence from the council`
    ELSE `the teacher must` `attend the pedagogical council`

-- 9 ¶2: she also attends any other meeting the principal calls for a special
-- need, outside the council's fixed times too, the opening and closing of the
-- year included; the principal takes into account whether a part-time
-- teacher can attend.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_9/p2
GIVEN `works part-time` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.9 meetings the principal calls` `works part-time` IS
    `the teacher must` `attend a meeting the principal called for a special need`
    RAND (IF `works part-time`
          THEN `the principal must` `take into account a part-time teacher's ability to attend`
          ELSE FULFILLED)

-- 10: a teacher teaching under half a position in the school is bound only to
-- the meetings where questions of her work in the school are discussed.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_10
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `the meeting concerns her work` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bound to attend` `position fraction` `the meeting concerns her work` IF
    `position fraction` AT LEAST 0.5 OR `the meeting concerns her work`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_11
GIVEN `a matter within the council's authority` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.11 the council's decisions bind` `a matter within the council's authority` IS
    IF `a matter within the council's authority`
    THEN `the teacher must` `follow the pedagogical council's decisions`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_12
GIVEN `the principal and the council's majority disagree` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.12 reconsideration` `the principal and the council's majority disagree` IS
    IF `the principal and the council's majority disagree`
    THEN PARTY `the pedagogical council`
         MUST  `reconsider the disagreement with the supervisor present`
         LEST  BREACH BY `the pedagogical council` BECAUSE "3.3.12: a disagreement between the principal and the council's majority is reconsidered with the supervisor"
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_13 akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_13/p2
GIVEN `teaches in the classes of that small council` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.13 small pedagogical councils` `teaches in the classes of that small council` IS
    IF `teaches in the classes of that small council`
    THEN `the teacher must` `attend the small pedagogical council`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `9 and 10 together`

-- A council meeting binds the teacher 10 binds; she then attends, or tells
-- the principal in advance why she cannot.
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER, `the meeting concerns her work` IS A BOOLEAN, `a justified reason to miss it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `a council meeting, for a teacher of any position` `position fraction` `the meeting concerns her work` `a justified reason to miss it` IS
    IF `bound to attend` `position fraction` `the meeting concerns her work`
    THEN `3.3.9 the pedagogical council` `a justified reason to miss it`
    ELSE FULFILLED

§§ `14-18 Duties at school`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_14
`3.3.14 duty rosters` MEANS `the teacher must` `do the duty roster the principal set`

-- 15: at least five minutes before school or her first lesson.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_15
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.15 punctuality` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `be at school before the start` m PROVIDED m AT LEAST 5
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "3.3.15: at school at least 5 minutes before the start"

-- 16א: a teacher with more than half a position, at least, takes part, as
-- part of her work, in the activities the school organises for its pupils
-- (trips, theatres, exhibitions). F-3.3-b: "למעלה מחצי משרה, לפחות" — more
-- than half, or at least half? The reading adopted: at least half.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_16__subpara_a
GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.16א pupils' activities` `position fraction` IS
    IF `bound to take part in pupils' activities` `position fraction`
    THEN `the teacher must` `take part, as part of her work, in the activities the school organises for its pupils`
    ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN `position fraction` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `bound to take part in pupils' activities` `position fraction` IF
    `position fraction` AT LEAST 0.5

`"more than half, at least" reads two ways at half a position` MEANS
        `bound to take part in pupils' activities` 0.5
    AND NOT 0.5 GREATER THAN 0.5
#ASSERT `"more than half, at least" reads two ways at half a position`

-- 16ב: every teacher accepts the post of class educator if asked, save one
-- teaching under 10 lessons a week in the school — unless she teaches the
-- class she would educate "at least 6 to 8 lessons" (F-3.3-a). A full-timer
-- teaching in two schools or more is made an educator only where she
-- teaches most of her hours.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_16__subpara_b
GIVEN `asked to be a class educator` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lessons a week in the school` IS A NUMBER
      `lessons in the class she would educate` IS A NUMBER
      `full-time in two schools or more` IS A BOOLEAN
      `this school has most of her hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.16ב class education` `asked to be a class educator` `lessons a week in the school` `lessons in the class she would educate` `full-time in two schools or more` `this school has most of her hours` IS
    IF     `asked to be a class educator`
       AND (NOT `exempt under 3.3.16ב` `lessons a week in the school` `lessons in the class she would educate`)
       AND `may be made an educator in this school` `full-time in two schools or more` `this school has most of her hours`
    THEN `the teacher must` `accept the post of class educator`
    ELSE FULFILLED

GIVEN `lessons a week in the school` IS A NUMBER, `lessons in the class she would educate` IS A NUMBER, threshold IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exempt from educating a class` `lessons a week in the school` `lessons in the class she would educate` threshold IF
    `lessons a week in the school` LESS THAN 10 AND `lessons in the class she would educate` LESS THAN threshold

-- The reading adopted: the lower figure, 6, is the threshold (the exception
-- is read widely, so the duty reaches the teacher who teaches the class 6
-- lessons or more).
GIVEN `lessons a week in the school` IS A NUMBER, `lessons in the class she would educate` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `exempt under 3.3.16ב` `lessons a week in the school` `lessons in the class she would educate` IF
    `exempt from educating a class` `lessons a week in the school` `lessons in the class she would educate` 6

`"at least 6 to 8 lessons" decides a teacher of 7 lessons both ways` MEANS
        NOT `exempt from educating a class` 9 7 6
    AND `exempt from educating a class` 9 7 8
#ASSERT `"at least 6 to 8 lessons" decides a teacher of 7 lessons both ways`

GIVEN `full-time in two schools or more` IS A BOOLEAN, `this school has most of her hours` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `may be made an educator in this school` `full-time in two schools or more` `this school has most of her hours` IF
    (NOT `full-time in two schools or more`) OR `this school has most of her hours`

-- 17א: every teacher, subject teachers included, receives parents at least
-- once a trimester and reports on the pupils' achievements in her subjects.
-- Time in trimesters.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_17__subpara_a
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.17א receiving parents` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `receive parents and report on achievements`
    WITHIN 1
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "3.3.17א: at least once a trimester the teacher receives parents"

-- 17ב: no answering parents or outsiders during lessons, nor at other times
-- unless she set them in advance.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_17__subpara_b
`3.3.17ב answering parents and outsiders` MEANS
    `the teacher shall not` `answer parents or outsiders during lessons`
    RAND `the teacher shall not` `answer parents or outsiders at another time she did not set in advance`

-- 18: the teacher answers the principal's call to substitute, save for
-- sufficient reason to refuse; one freed on a day by a pupils' trip stays
-- at school in those hours, at the principal's disposal, and substitutes as
-- needed, unpaid.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_18
GIVEN `the principal asks her to substitute` IS A BOOLEAN, `sufficient reason to refuse` IS A BOOLEAN, `freed by a pupils' trip` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.18 substitution` `the principal asks her to substitute` `sufficient reason to refuse` `freed by a pupils' trip` IS
    (IF `the principal asks her to substitute` AND (NOT `sufficient reason to refuse`)
     THEN `the teacher must` `substitute for a missing teacher`
     ELSE FULFILLED)
    RAND
    (IF `freed by a pupils' trip`
     THEN `the teacher must` `stay at school in the freed hours at the principal's disposal and substitute as needed`
     ELSE FULFILLED)

`pay for substituting in hours freed by a pupils' trip` MEANS 0

§§ `19-25 Confidentiality and pupils`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_19
`3.3.19 the council's confidentiality` MEANS `the teacher shall not` `disclose the pedagogical council's discussions to a non-member without the principal's consent`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_20__subpara_a
`3.3.20א pupils' details` MEANS `the teacher shall not` `disclose details about pupils to anyone but the principal, the class educator or the parents or guardians`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_20__subpara_b
`3.3.20ב documents of the school` MEANS `the teacher shall not` `issue a confirmation or document that may be seen as the school's without the principal's consent`

-- 21 prints "the teacher shall invite guests and visitors … except with the
-- principal's approval"; the "except" shows the dropped "not", and it is
-- read as a prohibition.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_21
`3.3.21 guests` MEANS `the teacher shall not` `invite guests or visitors to the school or class without the principal's approval`

-- 22: notice of an absence as early as possible, at the latest in the morning
-- of its first day before school starts. Time in minutes from midnight of
-- that day; the start is an input.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_22
GIVEN `minute school starts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.22 notice of absence` `minute school starts` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    MUST  `notify the principal of an absence`
    WITHIN `minute school starts`
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "3.3.22: the principal is told of an absence before school starts on its first day"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_23
GIVEN `serious indiscipline in her lesson requires removing a pupil` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.23 serious indiscipline` `serious indiscipline in her lesson requires removing a pupil` IS
    IF `serious indiscipline in her lesson requires removing a pupil`
    THEN `the teacher must` `refer the pupil to the class educator or the school's management`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_24__subpara_a
`3.3.24א sending a pupil home` MEANS `the teacher shall not` `send a pupil home during lessons without the principal's consent and notice to the parents`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_24__subpara_b
`3.3.24ב never for homework, lateness or a donation` MEANS `the teacher shall not` `send a pupil home for homework, lateness or a donation`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_25
`3.3.25 grades are not punishment` MEANS `the teacher shall not` `lower a grade as a punishment`

§§ `26-31 General`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_26
`3.3.26 within the guidelines` MEANS `the teacher must` `follow the Ministry's guidelines, the principal and the council`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_27
`3.3.27 training` MEANS `the teacher must` `take part in training in free time`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_28
`3.3.28 gifts` MEANS `the teacher shall not` `accept from pupils or parents a gift of benefit that is not a symbolic token of thanks`

-- 29א: no paid private lessons to pupils of her school — save as 29ב allows:
-- in a locality with one school, with the supervisor's approval.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_29__subpara_a
GIVEN `the only school in the locality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.29א private lessons` `the only school in the locality` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    SHANT `give paid private lessons to pupils of her school` `the supervisor approved` PROVIDED (NOT `the only school in the locality`) OR (NOT `the supervisor approved`)
    LEST  BREACH BY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee` BECAUSE "3.3.29א: no paid private lessons to pupils of her school"

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_29__subpara_b
GIVEN `the only school in the locality` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.29ב the only school in the locality` `the only school in the locality` IS
    IF `the only school in the locality`
    THEN PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
         MAY   `give paid private lessons to pupils of her school` `the supervisor approved` PROVIDED `the supervisor approved`
    ELSE FULFILLED

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_29__subpara_c
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.29ג organised groups` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `teach organised school groups for pay` `the supervisor approved` PROVIDED `the supervisor approved`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_30__subpara_a
`3.3.30א smoking` MEANS `the teacher shall not` `smoke in the institution before the pupils while on duty`

-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_30__subpara_b Points to the attached extension of the order against smoking in public places to educational institutions, a linked document not in this text.

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_31__subpara_a
`3.3.31א the press` MEANS `the teacher shall not` `publish in the press information on her work, post or institution, directly or through another, named or not, without leave of the director-general or his delegate`

@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_31__subpara_b
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.31ב articles and books` IS
    PARTY `a takanon party` `the teaching employee`
    MAY   `write articles or publish books on her educational work, keeping confidentiality`

-- 31ג: a teacher who thinks the public should hear of an important event in
-- the institution's life passes it through the district manager to the
-- spokesman's office, which publishes it as needed.
@ref akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_2__para_31__subpara_c
GIVEN `thinks the public should hear of an event in the institution` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A DEONTIC `3.3 party` `teacher's act`
DECIDE `3.3.31ג news of the institution` `thinks the public should hear of an event in the institution` IS
    IF `thinks the public should hear of an event in the institution`
    THEN `the teacher must` `pass news of the institution to the spokesman through the district manager`
    ELSE FULFILLED

-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_3 The heading of the source list (אסמכתא).
-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_3/p1 A source: "post holders in the elementary school" (February 1975) and special director-general's circular ו' (5755).
-- akn:chp_3__sec_3_3__hc_3/p2 A source: special director-general's circular ו' (5755), sections 1-2.

